          %h6#71ii_modules_over_groupoids 7.1.ii Modules over groupoids
          %p
            A
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+groupoid"} module over a groupoid
            is a collection of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
          .un_def
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong (module over a groupoid)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} = (\mathcal{G}_1 \stackrel{\to}{\to} \mathcal{G}_0)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              %strong module over the groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              is a collection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{N_x\}_{x \in \mathcal{G}_0}
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi x
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N_x \times \mathcal{G}(x,y) \to N_y
            %p that are linear and respect the groupoid composition in the obvious way.
          %h6#71iii_the_category_of_crossed_complexes 7.1.iii The category of crossed complexes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
          %h6#71iv_homotopy_and_homology_groups_of_crossed_complexes 7.1.iv Homotopy and homology groups of crossed complexes
          %p (…)
          %h6#FundamentalCrossedComplex 7.1.v The fundamental crossed complex functor
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            generalizes to a notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "-groupoid." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+space"} filtered space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_*
            one can consider the variant where the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_k
            %em fundamental crossed complex
            of a filtered space is the equivalent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
            incarnation of the fundamental strict
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .un_def
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (fundamental crossed complex)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+space"} filtered space
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X_1,X_0)
              for the subgroupoid of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X_1)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              on objects that are in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            %p
              The
              %strong fundamental crossed complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi X_*
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
            %p with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Pi X_*)_1 = \Pi_1(X_1,X_0)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi for
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Pi X_*)_n
                    \:=
                    \\coprod_{x \in X_0}
                    \\pi_n(X_n, X_{n-1}, x)
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    for n \geq 2
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X_n, X_{n-1}, x)
              is the
              %span.newWikiWord
                relative homotopy group
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/relative+homotopy+group"} ?
              obtained by equivalence classes of maps from the pointed
              = succeed "-disk" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that the disk lands in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n-1}
              and its basepoint on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %p See also section 1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"}> Ronnie Brown
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rafael+Sivera"} Rafael Sivera
              %em Normalization of the fundamental crossed complex of a simplicial set
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0611728"}> arXiv:math/0611728
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.63.9955&rep=rep1&type=pdf"} pdf
          .un_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (fundamental crossed complex of the
                = succeed "-simplex)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p
              The topological
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
              is canonically a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+space"} filtered space
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta^n)_k
              being the union of its
              = succeed "-faces." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %p
              Then we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1((\Delta^n)_1, (\Delta^n)_0)
              is the groupoid whose objects are the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
              vertices of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
              and which has precisely one morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i \to x_j
              for each ordered pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi j
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i,x_j \in (\Delta^n)_0
              (all of them being
              = succeed "s)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↗
                              %mo ↙
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                              %mo ↖
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mo ←
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 2
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi_1((\Delta^2)_1,(\Delta^2)_0) =
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; x_1
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow \nwarrow
                    \\\
                    x_0 &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}&amp;&amp; x_2
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              At any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
              the relative homotopy group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_2((\Delta^n)_2,(\Delta^n)_1, x_i)
              is a group on the set of 2-faces that have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
              as a 0-face: there is a unique homotopy class of disks in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
              that sits in the 2-faces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta^n)_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_j
              and whose boundary runs along the boundary of a given 2-face of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
            %p
              So (using the equivalence of crossed complexes with strict
              = succeed "-groupoids)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi \Delta^2
              is generated from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1((\Delta^2)_1,(\Delta^2)_0)
              as above and a 2-cell
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; x_1
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \swarrow &amp;\Downarrow&amp; \nwarrow
                    \\\
                    x_0 &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; x_2
                    }
            %p
              under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/whiskering"} whiskering
              and composition. For instance
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/whiskering"} whiskering
              this with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 \to x_2
              yields the 2-morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇙
